/**
 * Feed source adapter (ADR-0020).
 *
 * The pipeline does NOT own feed data. It consumes articles through this
 * pluggable boundary. Initial implementation is the `feedq` CLI tool from
 * the feed service repo (see feedq-adapter.ts). Other adapters (RSS, file,
 * gRPC, in-memory test fixtures) implement the same shape.
 *
 * Contract:
 *   - article_ref  : the article's one public identity, minted once by Feed
 *                    (feed ADR-0004: `art-<yyyymmdd>-<hex8>`). The adapter
 *                    only relays this value; it never derives its own
 *                    identity for feed content.
 *   - revision     : the revision this row reflects (feed ADR-0005). A
 *                    live-update article keeps the same article_ref across
 *                    rescans and increments revision when its body changes.
 *   - body         — full article text. The pipeline chunks in-memory; the
 *                    source MUST NOT do automated chunking on our behalf.
 *
 * Cache invalidation for extract/classify does NOT read a source-provided
 * hash: the extract step computes its own content hash over the
 * prompt-visible, post-chunking article projection (see
 * `computeExtractCacheContentHash` in `agents/pipeline/steps/extract.ts`).
